Root cause:
The bug was caused by the hotplug detection and notification being handled directly within the IRQ handler, which could block the processing of further IRQ events due to potential mutex contention. This led to delays in handling important events like EDID readiness during boot, as the IRQ handler was unable to complete its execution while waiting for the mutex, resulting in missed or delayed hotplug notifications.
